            <ArticleTitle>Cutting balloon inflation for drug-eluting stent underexpansion due to unrecognized coronary arterial calcification.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>185-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Unrecognized calcification is a cause of stent underexpansion which significantly increases the subsequent risks of restenosis and/or stent thrombosis. We describe the use of cutting balloon inflation within the implanted stent which overcame calcific restraint unresponsive to high pressure inflations with non-compliant balloons.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
